                <pb facs="0434" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3243: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Feely</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-25T11:00:00-04:00">July 25, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 25—11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. Referring to my telegram No. 61, July 15, 11 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >p.m.?</hi>], the Bolivian Government yesterday instructed its delegation to
                    request that the League give a mandate to the ABCP countries to organize a
                    commission of investigation and to make proposals for an arbitral <hi
                        rendition="#italic">compromis</hi> to the belligerents. The Bolivian
                    Government is informed that the Paraguayan delegation has received identic
                    instructions, and is hopeful that in view of the impasse in Geneva the <pb
                        facs="0435" n="347" xml:id="pg347"/> League will accede to the request. The
                    preliminary negotiations resulting in this action took place in Rio de Janeiro
                    under the auspices of the Brazilian Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Feely</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
